// Formal artifacts and the implementation functions each one models
// (verification pipeline plan §2-5 ①). `hash` is the FNV-1a 64 hash of
// the listed functions' tokens, `fn` to closing brace, comments, doc
// comments and whitespace excluded, in the order listed. The lint rule
// formal-drift reports an entry whose functions no longer hash to it;
// `zig build lint -Dlint-print-hashes` prints the current values.
// `checked_against` says what the artifact was actually checked against,
// so that a matching hash is not read as "the artifact verifies this code".
.{
    .{
        .artifact = "formal/lean/ZigpropFormal/Normalize.lean",
        .impl = .{.{ .file = "src/source.zig", .func = "draw" }},
        .hash = 0x206a3c2320106aa8,
        .checked_against = "design v2 (§2, MF1): `normalize` over Nat models the replay rule in Source.draw's .replay branch (bound 0 verbatim, else raw % bound). The Lean header names Source.draw's .replay branch, the path every Source primitive goes through (`range` is declared twice in src/source.zig, so draw is also the unambiguous name here). Bridge.lean proves that a UInt64 model of the replay line agrees with normalize on toNat images (normalizeU_toNat, so no u64 overflow or wrap changes the result); that draw implements that model is argued, not proved. Not re-checked against v2.1 or v0.3.",
    },
    .{
        .artifact = "formal/lean/ZigpropFormal/Zigzag.lean",
        .impl = .{
            .{ .file = "src/gen.zig", .func = "rankToValue" },
            .{ .file = "src/gen.zig", .func = "valueToRank" },
        },
        .hash = 0x6e7d3e0d952d1a55,
        .checked_against = "design v2 (§4.1): zigzagEncode/zigzagDecode over Int/Nat model the signed-integer rank map in rankToValue (decode) and valueToRank (encode). Bridge.lean proves, about Lean models, that the Zig-side signed rank maps equal zigzagEncode/zigzagDecode, that signed width-W values (W <= 64) and ranks below 2^W correspond, and that those ranks fit u64; that rankToValue/valueToRank implement these models, and @intCast safety at the Zig level, are argued, not proved. Float ranks (floatRankToValue) are a different encoding and not modelled; not re-checked against v0.3.",
    },
    .{
        .artifact = "formal/lean/ZigpropFormal/Shortlex.lean",
        .impl = .{
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "keyShortlexLess" },
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "tryAccept" },
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "tryRatchet" },
        },
        .hash = 0xdf3eeeff5e2b32e5,
        .checked_against = "design v2 (pre-v2.1): shortlex as a strict order on List Nat values, and well-founded (shortlex_wf, lex_wf_of_length). The implementation compares skip-filtered u64 key sequences (v2.1, keyShortlexLess via tryAccept); Bridge.lean proves that a UInt64 model of that comparison equals shortlex over the filtered, toNat-mapped lists, while that keyShortlexLess implements the model is argued, not proved, and tryRatchet's lateral move is in Measure.lean, not here. Not re-checked against v0.3.",
    },
    .{
        .artifact = "formal/lean/ZigpropFormal/Measure.lean",
        .impl = .{
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "tryAccept" },
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "tryRatchet" },
        },
        .hash = 0x61642f3ce381f566,
        .checked_against = "design v2.1 measure (key shortlex, pairs outside class 3): measureLt_wf proves the order well-founded over List Nat × Nat. accept_decreases and ratchet_decreases only restate their hypotheses; that tryAccept and tryRatchet lower the measure is observed by the accept hook in tests/meta9.zig, not proved. Bridge.lean proves that a UInt64 model of keyShortlexLess equals key shortlex over Nat (keyLess_iff_shortlex); that the Zig function is that model is argued, not proved.",
    },
    .{
        .artifact = "formal/lean/ZigpropFormal/Bridge.lean",
        .impl = .{
            .{ .file = "src/source.zig", .func = "draw" },
            .{ .file = "src/gen.zig", .func = "rankToValue" },
            .{ .file = "src/gen.zig", .func = "valueToRank" },
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "keyShortlexLess" },
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "filteredLen" },
        },
        .hash = 0x50fc6140a8faed88,
        .checked_against = "design v0.4 §6.2: hand transcriptions over UInt64/Int, with claims proved about the Lean models only. draw: normalizeU transcribes the .replay line `if (bound == 0) raw else raw % bound`; normalizeU_toNat (equals normalize on toNat images, for all b v) and normalizeU_valid (Valid via normalize_always_valid); the .random branch, pos bookkeeping and the draw limit are not modelled. rankToValue/valueToRank: rankToValueI/valueToRankI transcribe the signed branches, with i128 as Int; rankToValueI_eq and valueToRankI_eq (equal zigzagDecode/zigzagEncode on all of Nat/Int), zigzagEncode_lt_pow and zigzagDecode_range (signed width-W values and ranks below 2^W correspond, 1 <= W <= 64), valueToRankI_fits_u64 (the rank is in [0, 2^64)) and valueToRank_i128_bound (the products stay inside i128); the unsigned branches, @intCast as Zig checks it, i128 wrap-around and float ranks are not modelled. keyShortlexLess/filteredLen: keyLess/keyLoop/filt, each side a list of (key, skip) pairs; keyLess_iff_shortlex (equals shortlex over the filtered, toNat-mapped key lists), keyLoop_eq_some (at equal filtered lengths the loop never reaches the unchecked b index) and keyLess_unskipped_iff_shortlex; the statement-by-statement fidelity argument is in the Bridge.lean header. filteredLen is a helper keyShortlexLess calls, listed so the hash covers it. That the Zig functions implement these models is argued by hand, not proved.",
    },
    .{
        .artifact = "formal/tla/ZigpropRunner.tla",
        .impl = .{
            .{ .file = "src/runner.zig", .func = "checkWith" },
            .{ .file = "src/shrink.zig", .func = "shrinkWith" },
        },
        .hash = 0xda439d1fb634d42b,
        .checked_against = "design v2 (§5-§7) + one v0.3 header note + P4 (v2.1) as ShrinkRatchet over a number nc: a finite rank abstraction of the runner/shrink protocol, not a refinement of the implementation; it does not check that tryRatchet counts or rewrites pairs as modelled. shrinkWith's hash covers every pass, since they are nested in its body. The hash was last moved by passChunks' u64-to-usize cast (32-bit build fix), which changes no value the model abstracts; the model was not re-checked for it.",
    },
}
